# Optional VS Code REST Client format. You can use curl, Postman or Insomnia instead.
# Reset the database first. Replace the base URL with your own local URL.
@base = http://localhost:8000/api/v1

### 1 List the first page: 200, IDs 1 and 2, total 8
GET {{base}}/items

### 2 Combine the category filter and page: 200, ID 7, total 3
GET {{base}}/items?category=camera&page=2

### 3 Missing item: 404 with a JSON error message
GET {{base}}/items/999

### 4 Create: 201 with the new item and a Location header
POST {{base}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Portable projector","category":"accessory"}

# After request 4, GET the URI in Location and confirm the same item is returned.
# You can also inspect the new row in MariaDB. Do not assume a particular new ID.

### 5 Reject a missing name: 400, with no inserted row
POST {{base}}/items
Content-Type: application/json

{"category":"camera"}
